TI  - Talk before they sleep: strategies for patient-centred communication in 
      anaesthesiology.
PG  - 934-939
LID - S0007-0912(24)00487-2 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.bja.2024.08.013 [doi]
AB  - Patient-physician communication is an integral part of daily anaesthetic 
      practice. Although it is an undeniably powerful means of building a solid 
      therapeutic alliance, several of its fundamental aspects are often overlooked, 
      which can hinder successful communication in the preoperative period. We outline 
      these underexploited elements by analysing the various phases of preoperative 
      patient-physician interactions to provide the practising anaesthesiologist with a 
      useful framework for achieving thoughtful and patient-centred communication.
