TI  - Understanding patient expectations around therapeutic benefits, risks, and the 
      chance of cure.
PG  - 410-412
LID - S0002-9610(18)31060-2 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.amjsurg.2018.08.012 [doi]
AB  - Conversations around surgical goals of care should focus on relational (e.g., 
      empathy, trust, understanding) instead of transactional processes (e.g., 
      communication). Rather than reducing the patient-surgeon relationship to isolated 
      variables such as "communication," a "relational lens" that considers all the 
      aspects of the patient-surgeon relationship and its dynamic processes is needed.
