TI  - I beg your pardon?! using conditionals theory to understand doctor-patient 
      communication problems.
PG  - e13470
LID - 10.1111/ijcp.13470 [doi]
AB  - BACKGROUND: Little attention is given to the process and impact of poor 
      communicaton on the doctor-patent relationship. OBJECTIVE: The paper aims to 
      employ Theory of Conditionals to help shed light on the experience from a patient 
      perspective. METHODS: Doesnt really apply as this was inductive research i.e. 
      based on other research in the area. RESULTS: Doesnt really apply except that The 
      Theory of Conditionals enables us to understand the points of mis-communication 
      as well as reasons behind misunderstandings across the medical consultation. 
      CONCLUSIONS: A number of recommmednations are made to support GPs to reduce the 
      impact of this problem on the medical consultation.
